entries.def:
γέεννα (γέενα, Mrk.9.45, Rec.), -ης, ἡ (perh. through Aram. גֵּיהִנָּם, from Heb. גֵּי הִנֹּם, Neh.11.30 גֵּי בֶּן־הִנֹּם, Jhn.18.16 גֵּי בּנֵי־הִנֹּם, 2Ki.23.10 valley of (the son, sons of) lamentation); 
[in LXX the nearest approach to γ. is γαίεννα, Jos.18.16 (Γαὶ Ὀννόμ, A), elsewhere φάραγξ Ὀνόμ (Jos.15.8, al.), V. Swete on Mrk.9.43 ;] 
Gehenna, a valley W. and S. of Jerusalem, which as the site of fire-worship…
